ly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.lem-fatal-gap-exclusion"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-fatal-gap-exclusion"],"id":"long.lem-fatal-gap-exclusion","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 6.37 (A greedy gap excludes every representation)","locator":"Long record Lemma 6.37, p. 54, label lem:fatal-gap-exclusion","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $d\\ge0$ be an integer and $u\\subseteq\\{1,\\ldots,d\\}$ a finite prefix. If\n$$\nX_u(2)+R_{d+1}<t<X_u(2)+w_{d+1},\n$$\nthen no support agreeing with $u$ through rank $d$ represents $t$: omitting $d+1$ leaves value at most the lower endpoint, while including it gives value at least the upper endpoint. Other length-$d$ prefixes have disjoint containing intervals by the first-difference argument using $w_n>R_n$. Since the displayed gap lies inside the interval for $u$, none of those prefixes can represent $t$ either. Thus a certified strict gap excludes every representation, not just one proposed continuation.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.lem-fatal-gap-exclusion","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.lem-fatal-gap-exclusion","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.lem-fatal-gap-exclusion%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.depth_prefix_interval_disjoint%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.lem-fatal-gap-exclusion%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.depth_prefix_interval_disjoint%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.ErdosProble